# API keys. runner.api_key() reads this; it must never be committed.
.env

# Raw model responses. Large, and regenerable from the checkpointed calls.
# Keep them out of git by default.
runs/
*.jsonl

# Resolved slugs and live pricing. Machine-generated, and the pricing goes stale
# within days, but the resolved_slug field is the only record of which build of
# each model was actually called. A reader who cannot see that cannot tell what
# was measured, and pilot_screen.py refuses to start without the file, so it is
# tracked. Read the prices as of 2026-08-09 and nothing later.
!models_resolved.json

# The report exists in the repository as a PDF. The .docx is the working file
# behind it and carries revision marks and comment anchors that are not evidence.
paper/*.docx

# Run logs and the local resume wrapper: operational, not evidence.
runs/*.log
runs/*.sh

# Generated reports
pilot_report.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# ...but the token measurement is the evidence the cost model rests on,
# so it is tracked. Without it estimate_cost.py cannot run.
!runs/
!runs/token_profile.jsonl

# Its reasoning-off counterpart. PROVENANCE argues the run should be fielded
# with reasoning off, on the grounds that it is closer to the conditions MSC25
# and KEELING24 ran under and that reasoning tokens inflate cost without
# entering the score. That is an empirical claim about token counts, and this
# 56-line file is the measurement it rests on. 148K.
!runs/token_profile_reasoning_off.jsonl

# The pilot is both: the cost model's primary source (estimate_cost.py reads it)
# and the record behind the inclusion decisions. 964K. Tracked for the same
# reason, and the report is the decision record it justifies.
!runs/pilot.jsonl
!pilot_report.md

# The study run itself. The earlier plan was to archive this beside the writeup
# rather than commit it; the analysis changed that. The paper's claim is about
# nonignorable missingness -- hermes truncating 32.3% of its responses, claude
# answering exactly 0 to every I4 question, the eight-model design being
# foreclosed rather than merely taxed -- and none of that is checkable from the
# scored array alone. A reviewer needs the responses the scoring rejected, which
# means the raw checkpoint has to be in the repository. 19M on disk, 2.0M packed.
#
# scores.npz is the assembled 8 x 5 x 15 x 5 array and scores_head.npz the
# head-on-truncation sensitivity; both are small and save re-running assemble.py
# to inspect a number.
!runs/study.jsonl
!runs/scores.npz
!runs/scores_head.npz

# The analysis outputs the report and the figures are built from. report_main.txt
# is the captured stdout of assemble.py and is what make_figures.py parses, so a
# reader who only wants the figures never has to re-run the assembler.
# results_extra.json holds the per-outcome coefficients, the decision study, the
# leave-one-out headlines and the response taxonomy. sensitivity.json records the
# two scoring perturbations and which of them leaves the design unchanged, and
# scores_logistic.npz is the array behind the one that does not.
!runs/report_main.txt
!runs/results_extra.json
!runs/sensitivity.json
!runs/scores_logistic.npz

# The null floor. 200 synthetic studies at the complete-case size, all five
# instruments driven by one planted utility profile per model. It took 797
# seconds to draw, so it is committed rather than left to be re-derived, and the
# .txt is the captured stdout that make_figures.py reads.
!runs/null_matched.npy
!runs/null_matched.txt
